-- title:
--   Pole clauses for the blown-up supersingular chart
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ and $\ell$ are primes and $M' \neq 0$ is a natural number, with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell \mid M'$ (`hℓM'`).
--
--   **Base field and level.** $L$ is a field of characteristic $0$, $\zeta \in L$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hζ`), and `hι` requires that some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ send $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is (`hH₁`) the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), which is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. The intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq L((X))$ is (`hK`) [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q^2*M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field generated by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   **Coefficient ring and the modular invariant.** $A$ is a henselian discrete valuation domain, an $L$-algebra with $L$ as its fraction field, with algebraically closed residue field; `hAq` puts $q$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and `hζA` requires $\zeta$ to lie in the image of $A$, and $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. The element $j \in K$ is nonzero and has (`hj`) Laurent series the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the classical $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Further, $\varpi$ generates the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies (`hϖt`) $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$.
--
--   Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, and let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **The Drinfeld-chart hypothesis `hArig`.** Let $X :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf A K j` over the middle algebra, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with `ιFin` the morphism from $\operatorname{Spec} C$. The hypothesis `hArig` asserts, for every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the global function coming from $\varpi$ via `toBase` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` sending $y'$ to $z$ and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ satisfying the supersingularity condition of `hss`, the existence of a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ carrying $\varpi$ to a generator of the maximal ideal of $W$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the form $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ being [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk of $X$ at $z$ onto $S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v - fu\big)$, subject to seven clauses, summarised here. Writing `toC` for the completion map on the stalk, `mkS` for the quotient map onto $S$, and `germY` for the homomorphism $C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ obtained from the chart $\operatorname{Spec} C$: (i) $e$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ every $\tau \in \operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) maps $C$ into $C$ — this predicate says that, read through any embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$, $\tau$ implements on quotients $f/g$ of weight-$k$ modular forms for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions the slash action of the matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹` $= \begin{pmatrix}\gamma_{00} & \gamma_{01}/q\\ q\gamma_{10} & \gamma_{11}\end{pmatrix}$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$; (iii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, such a $\tau$ induces on $C$ a map congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ as above inducing the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ intertwining $\tau|_C$ through $e \circ$ `toC` $\circ$ `germY`, fixing the classes of constants, satisfying $\theta(X_{j}) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$, and with $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$, with $c \equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, and with $c \not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (v) a separation clause: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1, P_2$ of $S$, each not containing both classes of $X_0, X_1$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and each containing an element of the form $a_i X_0 + b_i X_1 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to the stalk along $e \circ$ `toC` are distinct; (vi) an Igusa-type criterion: for a prime $P$ of $S$ not containing both classes of $X_0, X_1$, containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and containing some $X_0 + h$ with $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a \in C$ has `toC (germY a)` in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$; (vii) a Hasse clause: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the series obtained from the $j$-expansion by scaling all exponents by $q$, lies in $K$ and in $C$, and for some $a_0 \in A$ with the difference lying in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, some $e_0 \geq 1$ and some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$, the degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^i b^{e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W$ for all $a, b \in W$ not both in the maximal ideal with $a^qb - ab^q$ in the maximal ideal, and $e$ carries the germ of that difference to the class of $h$.
--
--   **The chosen point and its presentation.** Data $z$, $\varpi_z$ with `hϖz` identifying $\varpi_z$ as the germ at $z$ of $\varpi$ pulled back along `toBase`, `hz` placing $\varpi_z$ in the maximal ideal of the stalk, $y'$ with `hy'` and the supersingularity `hss'` for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, and `hy'y` : $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$, are fixed. Moreover a presentation of the above shape at $z$ is fixed: a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with `hσ₁`, series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and `hf₁` the congruence to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the completed stalk at $z$ onto $S_1 := W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1\big)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this presentation exactly the conjunction of the seven clauses (i)–(vii) above.
--
--   **The orbit ideal and the blow-up chart.** The ideal $J \subseteq C$ is (`hJ`) the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $(\tau|_C)^{-1}$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ$ `toC` $\circ$ `germY` of the ideal of $S_1$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, taken over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$. The $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ is (`hB`) the $A$-algebra underlying the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$.
--
--   **The local model.** $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and: `hR1` (two clauses) requires $C \le B$ and that every element of $K$ be a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \neq 0$; `hR2` (three clauses) requires $A \to B$ to be formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/(\varpi)$ to have Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) requires that an element of $L$ lie in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that the maximal ideal of $W$ be generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ be a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lie in $y$ exactly when it lies in the maximal ideal of $W$, and that $f \in K$ lie in $W$ exactly when $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h$ outside the maximal ideal of $W$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Two assertions hold.
--
--   First, there is an element $b \in B$ such that for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ whose intersection with $L$ consists exactly of the elements coming from $A$, and for which $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$ whenever it lies in $V$: if $j \in V$ and no value $p(j)$ of a monic polynomial $p$ over $A$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$, then $b \notin V$.
--
--   Second, for every maximal ideal $y''$ of $C$ containing $\varpi$ such that for no $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and no $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$ does the equivalence "$b \in y$ if and only if $\tau(b) \in y''$" hold for all $b \in C$ with $\tau(b) \in C$, there is an element $b \in B$ such that for all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, all $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$, and every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ which contains $C$ and for which every $c \in C$ with $\tau^{-1}(c) \in C$ and $\tau^{-1}(c) \in y''$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$, one has $b \notin V$.
--
--   This is the pole half of the construction of the auxiliary supersingular affine chart in the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-diamond frame: it produces in the blow-up algebra $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$ an element with a pole along every Igusa-type valuation (those for which $j$ has transcendental reduction) and, for each supersingular maximal ideal $y''$ outside the $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$-orbit of $y$, an element with a pole along every valuation centred at the translates of $y''$. It is used in the assembly of the supersingular affine chart with its ends, Hasse and orbit-pole data, and relies on the corresponding Igusa-pole and orbit-pole statements together with the power-of-the-uniformiser estimate for germs in the completed stalk.
